The trial run ({{date}}) finished {{pilot_days_early}} days before the day it was to start. As measured, the {{plan.runs}} baseline runs take {{x1.nights}} nights, running at night only ({{plan.night_hours}} hours a night) and keeping the runner's guard ({{plan.guard_limit_minutes}} minutes of AI working time within {{plan.guard_window_hours}} hours). If the AI working time of one run is twice the measured value it is {{x2.nights}} nights, and {{x4.nights}} nights at four times. To end inside the {{row_nights}} nights of {{row_start_md}}~{{row_end_md}}, that time must not exceed {{largest_minutes}} minutes on average ({{largest_factor}} times the measured value). Larger models and other tasks have not been measured yet.

The chance that the baseline measurement ends by {{row_end}} and the chance that the direction-fixing gate is reached by {{gate}} depend on the subscription capacity. In the schedule simulation the {{tasks_rolled}} tasks of the task breakdown were rolled {{sims}} times with each of {{n_seeds}} seeds for every case. From seed to seed the chances differ by up to {{noise.chances_move_up_to_points}} percentage points, the middle dates by up to {{noise.middle_dates_move_up_to_days}} days and the {{pct80}}% dates by up to {{noise.upper_dates_move_up_to_days}} days.

- At the plan's capacity (one account per AI company, about {{planning.days_a_week}} agent working days a week): the chance that the baseline measurement ends by that day was {{planning.before.p_baseline_by_row_end}}% with the inputs before the trial run; it is {{planning.finished_only.p_baseline_by_row_end}}% when finished work is only counted as finished, {{planning.numbers_only.p_baseline_by_row_end}}% when only the numbers measured in the trial run are entered, and {{planning.after_x1.p_baseline_by_row_end}}% with both (middle {{planning.after_x1.b_baseline.p50}}, {{pct80}}% {{planning.after_x1.b_baseline.p80}}). It is {{planning.after_x2.p_baseline_by_row_end}}% if the AI working time is twice the measured value and {{planning.after_x4.p_baseline_by_row_end}}% at four times. The chance of reaching the gate is {{planning.after_x1.p_gate_by_its_date}}% with both (middle {{planning.after_x1.g_dir.p50}}, {{pct80}}% {{planning.after_x1.g_dir.p80}}).
- Under today's conditions (one Claude account shared with the owner's other work, counted as about {{claude_shared.days_a_week}} agent working days a week): with both, the baseline measurement {{claude_shared.after_x1.p_baseline_by_row_end}}% (middle {{claude_shared.after_x1.b_baseline.p50}}, {{pct80}}% {{claude_shared.after_x1.b_baseline.p80}}), the gate {{claude_shared.after_x1.p_gate_by_its_date}}% (middle {{claude_shared.after_x1.g_dir.p50}}, {{pct80}}% {{claude_shared.after_x1.g_dir.p80}}).
- With one Claude account used for Dodam alone (counted as about {{claude_dedicated.days_a_week}} agent working days a week): with both, the baseline measurement {{claude_dedicated.after_x1.p_baseline_by_row_end}}% (middle {{claude_dedicated.after_x1.b_baseline.p50}}, {{pct80}}% {{claude_dedicated.after_x1.b_baseline.p80}}), the gate {{claude_dedicated.after_x1.p_gate_by_its_date}}% (middle {{claude_dedicated.after_x1.g_dir.p50}}, {{pct80}}% {{claude_dedicated.after_x1.g_dir.p80}}).

What one account gives in a week is an assumption, not a measured value. So the dates of {{row_month}} and of the rows after it stay as the plan's dates at the plan's capacity, and whether they move is judged after that amount has been measured. The time freed by finishing early goes to the {{plan.tasks}} tasks, to finishing the measuring tool and to the two measurements above.

